-- title:
--   Level-one period map for fake elliptic curves over ℂ
-- statement:
--   Let $q,q'$ be primes with $q'\neq q$ and $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ such that $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ is indefinite ($0<a$ or $0<b$) and, for every finite place $v$ of $\mathbb{Q}$, $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $v$ lies over $q$ or $q'$. Let $\Lambda$ be a maximal order (a finitely generated $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule containing $1$, closed under multiplication and spanning the algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$, maximal among such), let $\iota:\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\to M_2(\mathbb{R})$ be an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map, let $Fc_0$ be a field over $\mathbb{C}$ which is a curve over $\mathbb{C}$ in the sense of [`AlgebraicCurve.IsCurveOver`](def/AlgebraicCurve_IsCurveOver.html#L15) (principal divisors exist, all residue fields at places are finite over $\mathbb{C}$, and $\Omega_{Fc_0/\mathbb{C}}$ is free of rank one) and essentially of finite type, and let $U_0$ be a [`ModularCurve.UniformizedHeckeCurve`](def/ModularCurve_UniformizedHeckeCurve.html#L14) for the Fuchsian group `fuchsianGroup Λ ι`, the intersection of the image in $GL_2(\mathbb{R})$ under $\iota$ of the group generated by the units of $\Lambda$ with the kernel of the determinant; it carries a point map `U₀.pt` from $\mathbb{H}$ to places of $Fc_0$, a realisation map `U₀.realize`, and Hecke multisets `U₀.heckePoints`. The hypothesis $h_0$ collects: `U₀.pt` is surjective; for each prime $\ell$ there is a finite set $S\subseteq\Lambda$ of elements of reduced norm $\ell$, each of which, adelically as $x\otimes 1$, represents a member of `primeHeckeSet Λ ℓ` (written literally as `levelHeckeUSet Λ Λ ℓ` in the case $\ell\mid 1$), such that $S$ is a set of representatives for left multiplication by norm-one units of $\Lambda$ on the elements of $\Lambda$ of reduced norm $\ell$ with that adelic property, and such that the multiset `U₀.heckePoints ℓ`, mapped into $M_2(\mathbb{R})$, equals the image of $S$ under $\iota$; and that `U₀.realize` is a dictionary between $Fc_0$ and $\Gamma$-invariant meromorphic functions on $\mathbb{H}$: each realisation is meromorphic at every $\tau$, addition, multiplication and scalars from $\mathbb{C}$ are respected eventually on punctured neighbourhoods, realisations determine elements, are invariant under the Fuchsian group, and every $\Gamma$-invariant meromorphic function on $\mathbb{H}$ is realised. The conclusion asserts the existence of a map $\mathrm{per}$ from fake elliptic curves over $\mathbb{C}$ with $\Lambda$-action and level $1$ (`FakeEllipticCurve Λ 1 ℂ`) to $\mathbb{H}$ such that: (i) $E\cong E'$ in the sense of `FakeEllipticCurve.Iso` if and only if `U₀.pt` takes the same value at $\mathrm{per}(E)$ and $\mathrm{per}(E')$; (ii) for every prime $\ell$ distinct from $q$ and $q'$ and every $E$ there are $n$, a family $K:\mathrm{Fin}\,n\to E.\mathrm{ExtraLevel}\,\ell$ of extra $\ell$-level structures which are pairwise distinct and exhaust all extra $\ell$-level structures up to having the same points (equality of the `FactorsThrough` predicate on $\mathbb{C}$-points), and curves $d:\mathrm{Fin}\,n\to$ `FakeEllipticCurve Λ 1 ℂ` with $(E,K_i)$ related to $d_i$ by `FakeEllipticCurve.IsLevelIsogeny ℓ`, such that the multiset of places `U₀.pt (δ • per E)` for $\delta$ in `U₀.heckePoints ℓ` equals the multiset of places `U₀.pt (per (d i))`, $i$ ranging over $\mathrm{Fin}\,n$; and (iii) for $r\in\{q,q'\}$, if $E'$ is an Atkin–Lehner quotient of $E$ at $r$ in the sense of `FakeEllipticCurve.IsAtkinLehnerQuotient`, then the multiset of places `U₀.pt (δ • per E)` for $\delta$ in `U₀.heckePoints r` is the singleton $\{$`U₀.pt (per E')`$\}$.
--
--   This is the level-one case ($N=1$, $\Lambda$ maximal) of the complex uniformisation of the Shimura curve attached to an indefinite quaternion algebra ramified exactly at $\{q,q'\}$: fake elliptic curves over $\mathbb{C}$ with $\Lambda$-multiplication are parametrised by points of $\mathbb{H}$ modulo the Fuchsian group $\iota(\Lambda^{1})$, with $\ell$-level isogeny quotients matching the Hecke points and the Atkin–Lehner involutions at $q$ and $q'$ acting through a single Hecke point. It feeds the level-one points-and-correspondences statement [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.exists_uniformizedHeckeCurve_place_corr_single_eq_sum_levelOne_of_two_mul_dvd_neZero`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.exists_uniformizedHeckeCurve_place_corr_single_eq_sum_levelOne_of_two_mul_dvd_neZero).
